#######################
# help comments
#######################
usage ()
{
cat <<__EOM__
============diffusion processing pipeline for single job============
Usage: pipe_diff [options]
-------------------------------------------
Prerequisite:
   --datain	Input diffusion data
   --outdir	Output directory
   --t1dir	T1 working directory (providing dartel flow: "mri/y_*.nii")
Optional:
   --t1data	Input T1 data(used for normalization using CAT12 when dartel flow is not create)
   --model	diffusion model used to estimate the measures: dti(default),dki
   --fibmodel	diffusion model used to estimate the fiber orientation: dti(default),hardi,bedpostx
   --gradT	gradient transformation direction: -ix,-iy,-iz(default),-sxy,-syz,-szx
   --pipe	pipelines: full(default), prep,quant,track
   --voxsize	reslice voxel size in normalization
COMMENTS:
--Processing steps
Step[1]: Brain Extract(bet)
Step[2]: Motion and distortion correction(eddy_openmp)
Step[3]: DTI reconstruction(dtifit or dki_hyu)
Step[4]: Deterministic fiber orientation estimation (dtk)
Step[5]: Probabilistic fiber orientation estimation(bedpostx)
Step[6]: Spatial normalization estimation(bbr+dartel)
Step[7]: Write diffusion metrics into MNI space(using bbr+dartel)
--Pipelines
full:full step pipeline[1:7]
prep:preprocessing pipeline[1 2]
quant:quantification pipeline (VBA/TBSS),[1 2 3 6 7];
track:fiber tracking pipeline[1 2 3 4 6 7](dti,hardi) or [1 2 3 5 6 7](bedpostx);
Examples:
